.KEY DIR/A,STEP/K
.BRA {
.KET }
; amiga-pi install: C:amiga-pi, the pi coding agent. It stands alone: nothing here needs
; UP-Term, and nothing here looks at an UP-Term: assign (that would ask for the volume).
; Run by this archive's Install (an Installer script), which asks the questions:
;   Execute <archive>/Files/install.dos <archive>/Files [STEP <part>]
; From a Shell without Installer the same line installs everything. The Installer
; runs the parts one at a time with STEP (tests/test_dist_addons.py holds the two to
; the same list); the first part, check, has nothing to check for a stand-alone archive.
FailAt 21
; the archive's Files drawer: every name below is relative to it
CD "{DIR}"
If NOT "{STEP}" EQ ""
  Skip {STEP}
EndIf
; @include dist/common/@CHECKFRAG@
Lab pi
; C:amiga-pi, the pi coding agent (README): needs a TCP/IP stack, AmiSSL 5 for https;
; ENVARC:amiga-pi is where its settings go (Install never writes settings.json,
; models.json or auth.json); its data goes to UP-Term:var/amiga-pi
Copy amiga-pi C:amiga-pi CLONE QUIET
If NOT EXISTS ENVARC:amiga-pi
  MakeDir ENVARC:amiga-pi
EndIf
; CHANGELOG.md: what amiga-pi shows as What's New after an update and for /changelog. pi reads its own from its package directory; this
; archive's record drawer (ENVARC:upkg/amiga-pi, made by Install, removed whole by Uninstall) is where the program's own files
; are kept apart from the user's settings. A later Install replaces it. Nothing is written into ENVARC:amiga-pi.
MakeDir >NIL: @PKGDIR@ @RECORD@
Copy CHANGELOG.md @RECORDP@CHANGELOG.md CLONE QUIET
If NOT "{STEP}" EQ ""
  Quit 0
EndIf
Lab skills
; Agent Skills for the Amiga (README): one drawer per skill, installed beside the skills of the user. They go where amiga-pi
; keeps its growing data: UP-Term:var/amiga-pi/skills when there is an UP-Term: assign, else ENVARC:amiga-pi/skills (the loader
; reads both). Only the four drawers below are replaced (each one whole, so an update leaves no stale file); any other drawer
; in skills is the user's and is never touched. The autodocs are not part of this archive: the amiga-autodocs skill looks in the
; user's own NDK (assign NDK:).
Assign >NIL: UP-Term: EXISTS
If NOT WARN
  MakeDir >NIL: UP-Term:var UP-Term:var/amiga-pi UP-Term:var/amiga-pi/skills
  Delete >NIL: UP-Term:var/amiga-pi/skills/amigados ALL QUIET
  Copy skills/amigados UP-Term:var/amiga-pi/skills/amigados ALL CLONE QUIET
  Delete >NIL: UP-Term:var/amiga-pi/skills/arexx ALL QUIET
  Copy skills/arexx UP-Term:var/amiga-pi/skills/arexx ALL CLONE QUIET
  Delete >NIL: UP-Term:var/amiga-pi/skills/amiga-c-build ALL QUIET
  Copy skills/amiga-c-build UP-Term:var/amiga-pi/skills/amiga-c-build ALL CLONE QUIET
  Delete >NIL: UP-Term:var/amiga-pi/skills/amiga-autodocs ALL QUIET
  Copy skills/amiga-autodocs UP-Term:var/amiga-pi/skills/amiga-autodocs ALL CLONE QUIET
Else
  MakeDir >NIL: ENVARC:amiga-pi ENVARC:amiga-pi/skills
  Delete >NIL: ENVARC:amiga-pi/skills/amigados ALL QUIET
  Copy skills/amigados ENVARC:amiga-pi/skills/amigados ALL CLONE QUIET
  Delete >NIL: ENVARC:amiga-pi/skills/arexx ALL QUIET
  Copy skills/arexx ENVARC:amiga-pi/skills/arexx ALL CLONE QUIET
  Delete >NIL: ENVARC:amiga-pi/skills/amiga-c-build ALL QUIET
  Copy skills/amiga-c-build ENVARC:amiga-pi/skills/amiga-c-build ALL CLONE QUIET
  Delete >NIL: ENVARC:amiga-pi/skills/amiga-autodocs ALL QUIET
  Copy skills/amiga-autodocs ENVARC:amiga-pi/skills/amiga-autodocs ALL CLONE QUIET
EndIf
If NOT "{STEP}" EQ ""
  Quit 0
EndIf
Lab launch
; Quick-launch icons: double-click one in UP-Term: to open an UP-Term window running the app
; (IconX opens the XCON: window; it closes when the app ends).
; Stand-alone archive: with no UP-Term: assign there is no UP-Term window and no UP-Term: drawer to
; put them in (XCON: is the UP-Term handler), so nothing is installed and nothing named UP-Term: is touched.
Assign >NIL: UP-Term: EXISTS
If NOT WARN
  Copy "launch/amiga-pi" "launch/amiga-pi.info" UP-Term: CLONE QUIET
EndIf
If NOT "{STEP}" EQ ""
  Quit 0
EndIf
; @include dist/common/record.dos
Echo "amiga-pi installed: type  amiga-pi  in a Shell or an UP-Term window."
